# Line endings are repo state, not a per-developer git setting.
#
# This repo is the reason the rule matters. The artifact writers in
# experiment.py, real_experiment.py and report.py pass newline="\n" so their
# JSON is byte-identical across platforms, and check_documented_metrics.py
# asserts on those committed bytes. That fix pins what the *writers* emit;
# this file pins what *git* stores and checks out, which is the other half.
# Without it, a clone with core.autocrlf=true would materialise the committed
# artifacts with CRLF and the guard would compare re-flowed bytes.
* text eol=lf

# report.py writes a .parquet into artifacts/ alongside the JSON that IS
# committed, and .gitignore un-ignores files in that directory one by one --
# so the parquet is a single `git add -f` away from being tracked. Declared
# binary now, because the `text` rule above would otherwise strip CR bytes
# out of it on commit and corrupt it silently.
*.parquet binary
